{"entryId":"1601","paragraphs":[{"sourceId":"heilprin:sefaria-warsaw:ta:1601:1","sourceSha256":"ea13edb4a8080547cd4a7e531d674cc90430537da030952e61f4c0b16af27a53","englishSha256":"16d89e799968b9a702410ed4201625a953982cb97bd7734f194ed5d8557a1b40","citations":[{"id":"1601:1:citation-01","he":[9,35],"en":[11,70],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shir_HaShirim_Rabbah_1.15.4"},"reference":"Shir HaShirim Rabbah 1:15:4","assessment":"Exact first Chazit passage names Rabbi Taryai for the gates of Eden opening for the dove. The printed text’s Teraya and the compared vocalization remain visible.","evidence":[{"reference":"Shir HaShirim Rabbah 1:15:4","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shir_HaShirim_Rabbah_1.15.4"},"witness":"Midrash Rabbah -- TE"}]},{"id":"1601:1:citation-02","he":[37,66],"en":[75,125],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shir_HaShirim_Rabbah_4.1.2"},"reference":"Shir HaShirim Rabbah 4:1:2","assessment":"The second Chazit passage repeats Rabbi Taryai and the same gates-of-Eden teaching, in a distinct unit.","evidence":[{"reference":"Shir HaShirim Rabbah 4:1:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shir_HaShirim_Rabbah_4.1.2"},"witness":"Midrash Rabbah -- TE"}]},{"id":"1601:1:citation-03","he":[68,103],"en":[131,158],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bereshit_Rabbah_33.6"},"reference":"Bereshit Rabbah 33:6","assessment":"The exact Bereshit Rabbah parallel attributes the gates-of-Eden teaching to Rav Bibi directly.","evidence":[{"reference":"Bereshit Rabbah 33:6","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bereshit_Rabbah_33.6"},"witness":"Midrash Rabbah -- TE"}]},{"id":"1601:1:citation-04","he":[105,134],"en":[199,225],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Vayikra_Rabbah_31.10"},"reference":"Vayikra Rabbah 31:10","assessment":"The exact Vayikra Rabbah parallel gives Rabbi Berekhiah for the gates-of-Eden teaching, distinct from the other witnesses.","evidence":[{"reference":"Vayikra Rabbah 31:10","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Vayikra_Rabbah_31.10"},"witness":"Midrash Rabbah -- TE"}]}],"inlineHebrew":[0,1,2,3],"holds":[],"notes":[{"text":"Verified all four exact parallels of the dove bringing an olive leaf from Eden. Chazit gives Taryai in both places, Bereshit Rabbah gives Bibi, and Vayikra Rabbah gives Berekhiah. Preserve their distinct attributions.","references":[],"urls":[]}],"comparisonEvidence":[{"reference":"Shir HaShirim Rabbah 1:15:4","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shir_HaShirim_Rabbah_1.15.4"},"witness":"Midrash Rabbah -- TE"},{"reference":"Shir HaShirim Rabbah 4:1:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shir_HaShirim_Rabbah_4.1.2"},"witness":"Midrash Rabbah -- TE"},{"reference":"Bereshit Rabbah 33:6","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bereshit_Rabbah_33.6"},"witness":"Midrash Rabbah -- TE"},{"reference":"Vayikra Rabbah 31:10","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Vayikra_Rabbah_31.10"},"witness":"Midrash Rabbah -- TE"}]}],"entryEvidence":[]}
